import UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic
import UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness

/-!
# UGB.UnitalGroebner.unital_groebner_decomposition

**Real-content formalization** (replaces the former vacuous
`class … where holds : Prop`). The decomposition `A = I ⊕ Õ(G)` is
stated as a **concrete claim about the reduction system**: for a
Gröbner–Shirshov basis, every algebra element `f` decomposes as a
multi-step reduction `f →* nf` to a normal form `nf` (its
`Õ(G)`-component), and the deformed and graded algebras share the same
Hilbert function (flatness). Neither conjunct is instantiable with
`True`.

Content block
[`thm:main-theorem`](../../../unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem.md):
*Free module decomposition via unital Gröbner–Shirshov bases*.

## Manuscript statement

Let $R$ be a commutative ring with unity, $A$ an $R$-algebra free as an
$R$-module without quasi-zeros, $(B,<)$ an admissible system, and
$I \trianglelefteq A$ with a unital Gröbner–Shirshov basis $G$. With
$\widetilde{O}(G)$ the free $R$-module on the non-leading monomials,
(1) $A/I \cong \widetilde{O}(G)$ and (2) $A = I \oplus \widetilde{O}(G)$.

## What is weakened relative to the manuscript

The internal-direct-sum statement `A = I ⊕ Õ(G)` is rendered as its
two algorithmic consequences over the concrete `AlgElement` /
`RewritingSystem` types:

* **Õ(G)-component existence** — every `f` reduces (`MultiStepReduction`)
  to a normal form, i.e. an element supported on non-leading monomials;
  `f` minus this normal form lies in the ideal `I` generated by the
  rules. This is the `Õ(G)` summand of the decomposition.
* **Flatness** — `isFlat h_deformed h_graded`: the Hilbert function of
  the deformed algebra equals that of its associated graded, which is
  the dimension-count form of "no quasi-zeros / direct sum".

The `R`-module structure of the summands and the explicit `I`-component
are not formalized (raw `AlgElement` data type; see `AlgOps.lean` §6).
The existence/termination half is **proved** (bean qou-lzoo): it is
`normal_form_exists`, from `reduction_well_founded` plus the hypothesis
`hlc` that every rule has a unit leading coefficient. It used to invoke an
axiom of the same name that was not merely unproved but **false** — see
`NormalFormExistsRefutation`. The flatness half is still supplied by the
`gs_implies_flat` axiom of `Flatness.lean`.
-/

namespace UGB.UnitalGroebner

open UGB.GrobnerShirshov

universe u v

variable {G : Type u} {k : Type v}

/-- **Free-module decomposition — `Õ(G)`-component + flatness.**

    For a Gröbner–Shirshov basis `sys`, every element `f` reduces to a
    normal form (the `Õ(G)`-summand of `f` in `A = I ⊕ Õ(G)`), and the
    deformed/graded Hilbert functions agree (`isFlat`).

    The conclusion is a **concrete conjunction**: a `ReducesToNF`
    existential over `AlgElement` together with an `isFlat` equality of
    Hilbert functions — substantive content the former `holds : Prop`
    lacked. -/
-- Ref: [leitner2026] unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/main-theorem.ts
theorem unital_groebner_decomposition [Field k] [DecidableEq G]
    (ord : AdmissibleOrder G)
    (sys : RewritingSystem G k)
    (hgs : IsGrobnerShirshovBasis G k ord sys)
    (hlc : ∀ r ∈ sys.rules, IsUnit (r.lc ord))
    (h_deformed h_graded : HilbertFunction) :
    (∀ f : AlgElement G k, ∃ nf : AlgElement G k, ReducesToNF ord sys f nf) ∧
      isFlat h_deformed h_graded := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · -- Õ(G)-component: existence of a normal form for each f — now a theorem
    -- rather than the false axiom it used to invoke (bean qou-lzoo).
    --
    -- `hlc` is not decoration. Over a field it is *not* automatic: `lc` is the
    -- coefficient at the leading monomial of the `support` field, which is only
    -- a superset of the true support, so a rule can have `lc = 0`. Without it
    -- the conclusion is false — `NormalFormExistsRefutation` exhibits an `f`
    -- with no normal form for a system that satisfies `hgs`.
    intro f
    exact normal_form_exists ord sys hlc f
  · -- Flatness: discharged by the gs_implies_flat axiom of Flatness.lean
    -- (Hilbert function preserved under the GS deformation).
    exact gs_implies_flat ord sys hgs h_deformed h_graded

end UGB.UnitalGroebner
